1
00:00:07,961 --> 00:00:21,306
[SPEAKER_01]: Although living a virtuous, renunciate and secluded life, when I reflect about my day in the evenings, I feel like I have still been pushed around all day, despite not having failed in any of the aforementioned qualities.

2
00:00:21,326 --> 00:00:21,986
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is that?

3
00:00:22,606 --> 00:00:24,467
[SPEAKER_01]: How do I stop being pushed around?

4
00:00:28,089 --> 00:00:31,710
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, assuming that the questioner here is pushed around by his own mind,

5
00:00:33,028 --> 00:00:38,832
[SPEAKER_00]: Then it's good, of course, to be established in virtue, but that's not going to be enough now.

6
00:00:38,892 --> 00:00:40,233
[SPEAKER_00]: That is just the first step.

7
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:46,417
[SPEAKER_00]: So, keeping eight precepts is step one, but there's a lot of room within those

8
00:00:47,686 --> 00:00:52,868
[SPEAKER_00]: You still do all sorts of things that come out of your mind, pressuring you.

9
00:00:54,168 --> 00:00:58,009
[SPEAKER_00]: So, to establish yourself in the basic precepts, right?

10
00:00:58,110 --> 00:01:06,212
[SPEAKER_00]: Five plus celibacy and the non-distraction, that is the starting point for any serious mental development.

11
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:13,275
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, yes, you can adhere to those precepts externally, but the point is then twofold.

12
00:01:17,681 --> 00:01:24,005
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, the first point is that without establishing yourself in a precept, you're not even going to see your own mind.

13
00:01:25,366 --> 00:01:27,127
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you need to set up that boundary.

14
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:38,915
[SPEAKER_00]: Your mind will be running into it and that is where you can see, aha, I've been going in the wrong direction now and because I'm keeping these precepts, right, I've put up that fence and I'm determined to not go past it.

15
00:01:39,435 --> 00:01:43,038
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where you see your mind pushing you in that direction.

16
00:01:43,118 --> 00:01:46,300
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can catch a glimpse that you have been running with your mind.

17
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:55,346
[SPEAKER_00]: If you are at the point of breaking the precepts, you're not breaking it, but that's so... that container of the precepts is necessary to even see what your mind is.

18
00:01:55,886 --> 00:01:56,507
[SPEAKER_00]: That's their aim.

19
00:01:57,007 --> 00:02:14,140
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the second step is that you just don't want to be keeping it like that, but you now want to take that principle of understanding what it means to be pressured by your own mind, and you want to make that the sole criteria for whether something is wholesome or unwholesome.

20
00:02:15,128 --> 00:02:21,590
[SPEAKER_00]: So, every time you give in to the pressure of your mind, that is out of weakness on your part.

21
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:27,451
[SPEAKER_00]: And you have to then realize that the mind, citta, cannot actually force you to act.

22
00:02:27,851 --> 00:02:31,112
[SPEAKER_00]: It might feel like that, but you're always there with it, giving in.

23
00:02:32,733 --> 00:02:38,154
[SPEAKER_00]: So, out of carelessness, you can forget this right perspective and still go with the mind.

24
00:02:38,434 --> 00:02:39,855
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not good.

25
00:02:40,195 --> 00:02:44,156
[SPEAKER_00]: But, more importantly, we want to recognize, yeah, the mind cannot actually

26
00:02:45,641 --> 00:02:48,144
[SPEAKER_00]: force me to do things, I am there with it.

27
00:02:49,025 --> 00:02:55,631
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is why we often speak about taking or discerning this attitude of full complete responsibility.

28
00:02:55,651 --> 00:02:57,533
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, the whole thing is up to you.

29
00:03:01,855 --> 00:03:17,364
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, if you then externally keep the precepts, and you live a fairly secluded life, but at the end of the day you look back and you see, yeah, my mind was still bossing me around all day long, then that means that within the context of those precepts, you need to refine it further.

30
00:03:17,924 --> 00:03:30,572
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to look at your sensory strength, for example, like, which things am I attending through, eh, during my day, and just, eh, more generally,

31
00:03:32,645 --> 00:03:50,397
[SPEAKER_00]: Clarify what is mind, what does it mean to be pressured by my own mind, and am I still giving into that because I think it's too painful if I don't, or am I recognizing, no, the training is to not give in to the pressure of the mind, and then to recognize when the mind is pressuring you, which could be about

32
00:03:51,582 --> 00:03:54,043
[SPEAKER_00]: Something that is not at all covered by the precepts.

33
00:03:54,063 --> 00:03:54,744
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the thing.

34
00:03:55,164 --> 00:03:59,206
[SPEAKER_00]: In the beginning, it looks like, oof, it's a big challenge to even keep those eight precepts.

35
00:03:59,826 --> 00:04:01,447
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, that's the starting point.

36
00:04:02,027 --> 00:04:06,169
[SPEAKER_00]: At some point, you'll recognize, okay, I'm fairly solid now in keeping those precepts.

37
00:04:06,209 --> 00:04:09,671
[SPEAKER_00]: That that fence is getting more and more in the distance now.

38
00:04:09,691 --> 00:04:13,093
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not running into the fence the whole time anymore.

39
00:04:13,473 --> 00:04:15,334
[SPEAKER_00]: But, so, that's a good first step.

40
00:04:15,774 --> 00:04:17,095
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, you want to take it

41
00:04:20,778 --> 00:04:25,419
[SPEAKER_00]: More carefully, and want to look more closely, because what do those three steps cover?

42
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:29,821
[SPEAKER_00]: They cover your bodily behavior, and also your speech.

43
00:04:30,221 --> 00:04:35,243
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not lying, not any lewd speech, and so on.

44
00:04:35,643 --> 00:04:39,384
[SPEAKER_00]: But the actual purification now needs to happen on the

45
00:04:40,515 --> 00:04:57,722
[SPEAKER_00]: Mental level, what it is that you are thinking about, what it is that you accept and welcome and delight in mentally, or alternatively, all the things that you think shouldn't be there mentally and you want to get rid of, basically also hindrances, that's primarily on that level.

46
00:04:58,242 --> 00:05:01,283
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is still the mind pressuring you there.

47
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:10,628
[SPEAKER_00]: But you see, you're never gonna recognize any of that if the bodily and the verbal behavior is not restrained first.

48
00:05:11,208 --> 00:05:12,189
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's the first step.

49
00:05:12,590 --> 00:05:22,599
[SPEAKER_00]: And yeah, if you purify the stream, let's say, at the top of the mountain, then it's impossible that it becomes contaminated further downstream.

50
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:31,224
[SPEAKER_00]: But, eh... since we don't start in a neutral position, we first need to actually discern the whole origin of the stream, right?

51
00:05:31,264 --> 00:05:37,506
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is why yoniso, manasikāra is also a necessary factor for the arising of the right view.

52
00:05:37,886 --> 00:05:38,106
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

53
00:05:38,406 --> 00:05:43,728
[SPEAKER_00]: All of that begins by restraining bodily and verbal behavior, so that you even begin to see what is citta.

54
00:05:44,448 --> 00:06:00,727
[SPEAKER_00]: That which is pressuring you, as we talked about in the earlier discussion, and then you want to recognize that also on the mental level, on your, right, the thoughts that you welcome and delight in or want to get rid of, there too, citta is pressuring you.

55
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:05,503
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, there is also something as, let's say, mental discipline.

56
00:06:05,563 --> 00:06:09,307
[SPEAKER_00]: Keeping an eye on the kinds of thoughts that you welcome and delight.

57
00:06:09,968 --> 00:06:11,769
[SPEAKER_00]: And if they are sensual, you shouldn't do that.

58
00:06:12,490 --> 00:06:14,131
[SPEAKER_00]: You should not delight in those thoughts.

59
00:06:14,232 --> 00:06:15,453
[SPEAKER_00]: Cut them off.

60
00:06:15,493 --> 00:06:25,783
[SPEAKER_00]: If you're having entire conversations going on, that are rooted in annoyance, ill-will, aversion, why is this happening to me, self-pity, and all the rest of it.

61
00:06:26,523 --> 00:06:28,344
[SPEAKER_00]: That can go on for a while and you cannot notice it.

62
00:06:28,404 --> 00:06:34,845
[SPEAKER_00]: All of that is... there's still pressure behind that, behind those mental actions.

63
00:06:34,865 --> 00:06:39,926
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, it can be somewhat of a discovery to realize, wait, there is such a thing as mental action.

64
00:06:41,927 --> 00:06:47,108
[SPEAKER_00]: I can actually also just stop certain thoughts or at least not welcome and enlighten them.

65
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:52,509
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, I do have a responsibility also for what is going on mentally.

66
00:06:52,529 --> 00:06:54,110
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is what you now want to

67
00:06:55,455 --> 00:07:13,445
[SPEAKER_00]: Start looking into and developing, because if you do not welcome and delight anymore in thoughts of sensuality, if you do not welcome and delight ill-will, annoyance, thoughts of cruelty and so on, it's going to be impossible that by body and speech, anything of that kind is going to factually manifest.

68
00:07:13,485 --> 00:07:14,226
[SPEAKER_00]: This is impossible.

69
00:07:14,986 --> 00:07:23,051
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you tackle the problem there, right, you're moving, like, that whole fence is, like, properly in the distance now.

70
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:45,680
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, somebody can be established in virtue, by which I take it to mean he's just keeping the precepts externally, but to be accomplished in virtue, as the suttas often say, accomplished in virtue means that you are not just conforming to a set of rules externally, but you understand that what makes those rules

71
00:07:46,741 --> 00:07:47,722
[SPEAKER_00]: Why those rules are there?

72
00:07:47,862 --> 00:07:49,463
[SPEAKER_00]: What makes breaking them unwholesome?

73
00:07:49,843 --> 00:07:54,706
[SPEAKER_00]: Namely, that breaking any of those precepts means that you were totally overpowered by the pressure of your mind.

74
00:07:55,387 --> 00:07:57,448
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impossible to break those rules otherwise.

75
00:07:58,189 --> 00:08:00,210
[SPEAKER_00]: And so you want to understand the principle.

76
00:08:00,790 --> 00:08:06,414
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you see what makes something wholesome and unwholesome, which has nothing to do with what the world externally might think.

77
00:08:06,974 --> 00:08:10,477
[SPEAKER_00]: Has nothing to do with even specific sets of rules that you adhere to.

78
00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:19,454
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything that comes out of you giving in to the pressure of your own mind is unwholesome, even if it's not covered by the precepts.

79
00:08:20,754 --> 00:08:21,495
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the principle.

80
00:08:22,355 --> 00:08:30,179
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, understanding this principle means that whatever you do by body, speech and mind, you're gonna ask yourself, wait, why am I doing this now?

81
00:08:31,239 --> 00:08:33,700
[SPEAKER_00]: Why am I accepting, tolerating, going with this?

82
00:08:34,901 --> 00:08:36,882
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, why am I resisting this?

83
00:08:36,922 --> 00:08:39,063
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it mine that I ask for it, or is it just there?

84
00:08:39,956 --> 00:08:49,342
[SPEAKER_00]: And so you begin to question your involvement with those phenomena, and see, wait, I'm also responsible for my attitudes, for what I welcome and delight in, and what I want to get rid of.

85
00:08:52,483 --> 00:09:06,732
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you will go to experience more subtle manifestations of the same pressure, and the mind craving, that's what pressure is, and yeah, then mentally you shouldn't give in to that.

86
00:09:08,271 --> 00:09:20,374
[SPEAKER_00]: And by not giving in to those things mentally, if that becomes the level of your practice now, then at the end of the day, you will not feel that you have been bossed around by your own mind.

87
00:09:20,974 --> 00:09:30,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you haven't left any corners for your mind to be bossing you around, because you've now included that whole mental domain in your responsibility.

88
00:09:33,936 --> 00:09:42,738
[SPEAKER_01]: Would you say it's useful trying to discern first this principle of actually referring your actions always to your mind?

89
00:09:43,658 --> 00:09:57,842
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, throughout the day, any physical action, any verbal action, you actually first and foremost, obviously, it's within the precepts, let's assume, you first and foremost always look at your mind state, if there's any potential of

90
00:09:58,602 --> 00:10:18,204
[SPEAKER_01]: agitating the mind, if there's any potential that the mind pressures you towards it, even if it's something fairly wholesome, you could say, on the physical and verbal level, like studying, reading suttas, making a project, but you see the mind wants to do it, leaps towards it.

91
00:10:18,404 --> 00:10:18,645
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

92
00:10:19,465 --> 00:10:28,771
[SPEAKER_01]: And to actually pay attention to that tendency, because that's where, even within precepts, restraint and seclusion, the bossing around still happens.

93
00:10:29,151 --> 00:10:29,491
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

94
00:10:30,912 --> 00:10:37,736
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, with everything that you are doing, you have to ask yourself, wait, why am I doing this?

95
00:10:38,276 --> 00:10:39,797
[SPEAKER_00]: And why am I doing it specifically now?

96
00:10:40,798 --> 00:10:45,280
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then you can ask yourself, okay, what would happen if I'm not going to do it now?

97
00:10:46,508 --> 00:10:50,891
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, not so much like what are going to be the actual consequences on the world level.

98
00:10:50,991 --> 00:10:51,152
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

99
00:10:52,232 --> 00:10:55,095
[SPEAKER_00]: Is your mind going to make a dhamma about it if you don't do it now?

100
00:10:56,180 --> 00:11:02,602
[SPEAKER_00]: If it does, and you will be able to feel it, like, oh yeah, this is going to be a bit annoying if I'm not going to do this.

101
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:06,483
[SPEAKER_00]: That means that your mind is behind there, pressuring you to do it.

102
00:11:07,023 --> 00:11:08,163
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's when you should not do it.

103
00:11:08,863 --> 00:11:12,945
[SPEAKER_00]: And you see, it doesn't then even matter what it is that you're effectively going to do.

104
00:11:12,965 --> 00:11:13,125
[SPEAKER_00]: Right?

105
00:11:13,365 --> 00:11:15,645
[SPEAKER_00]: Not breaking any of the precepts, obviously.

106
00:11:16,325 --> 00:11:21,247
[SPEAKER_00]: But, and in the beginning, it might look like that everything that you do is coming out of the craving.

107
00:11:21,567 --> 00:11:21,767
[SPEAKER_00]: Like,

108
00:11:22,447 --> 00:11:29,692
[SPEAKER_00]: So, somebody hears, okay, mind is putting pressure on me, you take that message on, and then you realize, well, everything I do is coming out of pressure.

109
00:11:29,712 --> 00:11:35,717
[SPEAKER_00]: But that is just because the craving, the pressure, hasn't been discerned sufficiently accurately.

110
00:11:37,025 --> 00:11:39,066
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that is the refinement that needs to happen.

111
00:11:39,466 --> 00:11:53,811
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, the mind will be pushing you in some specific direction and then, the more you recognize that and do not give in to that pressure, the more you will begin to realize that there's actually a lot of space around it for other things to do that do now not come out of that pressure.

112
00:11:54,551 --> 00:11:55,932
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you can't do those things.

113
00:11:55,952 --> 00:11:56,893
[SPEAKER_00]: They're sort of parallel.

114
00:11:56,913 --> 00:12:01,216
[SPEAKER_00]: Your mind wants to pressure you this way, and you're just going to do something else that doesn't come out of the pressure.

115
00:12:01,576 --> 00:12:02,597
[SPEAKER_00]: The pressure is still there.

116
00:12:02,797 --> 00:12:05,559
[SPEAKER_00]: The pressure is saying, I want you to do this.

117
00:12:05,699 --> 00:12:07,220
[SPEAKER_00]: You start doing something else.

118
00:12:07,861 --> 00:12:11,203
[SPEAKER_00]: Meanwhile, keeping an eye on your mind, it still wants you to do this.

119
00:12:11,604 --> 00:12:15,426
[SPEAKER_00]: So, on the one hand, you resist the direction in which your mind wants to pressure you.

120
00:12:15,747 --> 00:12:18,509
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, which other thing you do, doesn't even matter all that much.

121
00:12:19,601 --> 00:12:22,225
[SPEAKER_00]: So you also become less concerned with what am I going to do.

122
00:12:22,245 --> 00:12:24,669
[SPEAKER_00]: The emphasis shifts to what am I not going to do.

123
00:12:25,491 --> 00:12:29,918
[SPEAKER_00]: But you see, next day, the thing that the mind is pressuring you to do now,

124
00:12:31,225 --> 00:12:35,588
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you could perhaps do it, because now the mind is not behind it pressuring you.

125
00:12:36,489 --> 00:12:44,836
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whether something is right or wrong for you on a certain occasion, is not determined by any sort of external code or conduct.

126
00:12:45,416 --> 00:12:55,544
[SPEAKER_00]: It's fully determined internally, by whether your mind is pushing you to do it, or whether you are in fact doing it, not out of weakness, because the mind is behind you, pressuring you.

127
00:12:57,103 --> 00:12:57,703
[SPEAKER_00]: And that means...

128
00:12:57,824 --> 00:13:03,728
[SPEAKER_00]: But you see, in order to now find out if it is okay to do this or not, you obviously need to see your mind.

129
00:13:04,849 --> 00:13:10,993
[SPEAKER_00]: And that you're only going to see when you start with the virtue, the restraint and the seclusion.

130
00:13:12,414 --> 00:13:16,537
[SPEAKER_00]: And the mind is not always putting pressure on you with the same thing.

131
00:13:17,098 --> 00:13:20,000
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this basically means that you have to be on the ball the whole time.

132
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:24,292
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's where the right mindfulness comes in.

133
00:13:24,713 --> 00:13:29,277
[SPEAKER_00]: The right mindfulness is, if I'm not going to do what I want to do now, it's going to be an issue.

134
00:13:30,197 --> 00:13:32,339
[SPEAKER_00]: Issue in relation to, will the mind take it?

135
00:13:32,639 --> 00:13:35,102
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it just going to be sort of, equanimous with it?

136
00:13:35,162 --> 00:13:37,423
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, oh, okay, we can do it some other time, no big deal.

137
00:13:38,004 --> 00:13:41,207
[SPEAKER_00]: Or is it going to be like, yeah, but I really want to do this sort of now.

138
00:13:42,087 --> 00:13:44,490
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you need to be in that sense,

139
00:13:45,971 --> 00:13:50,273
[SPEAKER_00]: More rational and say, well, this is not the right time to do it.

140
00:13:50,633 --> 00:13:52,314
[SPEAKER_00]: We might do it on some future occasion.

141
00:13:52,674 --> 00:13:53,095
[SPEAKER_00]: We don't know.

142
00:13:53,715 --> 00:13:54,155
[SPEAKER_00]: We will see.

143
00:13:56,116 --> 00:13:59,878
[SPEAKER_00]: And, yeah, that is all part of the training.

144
00:14:00,178 --> 00:14:13,605
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you will also recognize how futile it is to think that you can just train for an hour in the morning and an hour in the evening, because this just has to concern everything that you do 24-7, whether you're alone or with others, whether it's day or night.

145
00:14:14,485 --> 00:14:21,896
[SPEAKER_00]: Just as a parent is responsible for the child, and you cannot say, I'm going to be responsible for my child only for one hour in the morning and one hour in the evening, right?

146
00:14:22,116 --> 00:14:28,786
[SPEAKER_00]: Either you say, I'm bound up with this child, I need to look after it, or else, you're not a responsible parent.

147
00:14:33,676 --> 00:14:59,591
[SPEAKER_01]: And sometimes, when one isn't sure about, or one has the feeling, okay, this is probably not coming out of a pressure, the Buddha usually recommend as well, before, while, and after an action by body, speech and mind, to actually keep that context of, okay, you might have started off well, but actually while doing it, you realize the mind takes over, pressures you, and then you actually need to have the capacity to stop yourself in the middle of

148
00:15:00,727 --> 00:15:05,508
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, maybe a project that you really want to finish, but you say, hold on, I'm not going to do this now.

149
00:15:05,708 --> 00:15:08,249
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that was his advice to his own son.

150
00:15:08,829 --> 00:15:19,131
[SPEAKER_00]: For body, speech and mind, before you're going to do something, question, while you are engaged in those actions, because you see, while being engaged in an action, you can still stop and start doing something else.

151
00:15:20,012 --> 00:15:21,952
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you're the one who is acting.

152
00:15:22,472 --> 00:15:25,133
[SPEAKER_00]: And then afterwards, you can say, wait, did I not lose perspective?

153
00:15:25,833 --> 00:15:26,133
[SPEAKER_00]: Or not?

154
00:15:26,513 --> 00:15:29,954
[SPEAKER_00]: Or maybe it started out right, but somewhere it took a bit of a funny turn.

155
00:15:31,456 --> 00:15:36,398
[SPEAKER_00]: And yeah, that's useful to have some time at the end of the day to look back.

156
00:15:38,719 --> 00:15:45,182
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, in particular, like, you know, did I give in to pressure of the own mind or not?

157
00:15:45,722 --> 00:15:49,304
[SPEAKER_00]: And then to determine, well, I need to pay more attention next time.

158
00:15:49,324 --> 00:15:57,708
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you don't gain anything from living with a mind that is wild and not trained and tamed.

159
00:15:57,768 --> 00:15:58,008
[SPEAKER_00]: Because

160
00:16:00,450 --> 00:16:05,152
[SPEAKER_00]: At any moment, anything can happen and you will have to meet that situation with your mind.

161
00:16:05,872 --> 00:16:13,935
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the more the mind is opposed to you, the more difficult it will be for you to deal with the situation accurately.

162
00:16:14,075 --> 00:16:25,240
